{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1971 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d3115941a21fc2154e89c71e9f64a56ce5e3920a5c79a48108a41babba52c605" :edb/db-before-t 1970 :edb/db-after-t 1971 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535283 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:11:57.590Z" 13194139535283 true] [17592186096470 1100 "Which of the following sequences diverge?\n\n- $a_n = \\dfrac{1}{n^2}$ for $n \\geq 1$\n\n- $a_n  = \\dfrac{n^4}{2n^3+1}$ for $n \\geq 1$\n\n- $a_n = \\dfrac {3 n ^ 5 + 7} {5 n ^ 4 - 3 n ^ 3 }$ for $n\\geq 1?$" 13194139535283 true] [17592186096470 1100 "Which of the following sequences diverge?\n\n1. $a_n = \\dfrac{1}{n^2}$ for $n \\geq 1$\n2. $a_n = \\dfrac{n^4}{2n^3+1}$ for $n \\geq 1$\n3. $a_n = \\dfrac {3 n ^ 5 + 7} {5 n ^ 4 - 3 n ^ 3}$ for $n\\geq 1$?" 13194139535283 false] [17592186096470 1145 "Let's analyze each sequence in turn. We need to calculate the limit of each sequence as $n$ approaches at infinity.\n\n- In sequence I, the limit is\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} a_n = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\dfrac {1}{n^2} = 0.\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\n- In sequence II, the dominant term in the denominator is $2n^3,$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by $n^3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{4}}{2{n}^{3}+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{n}^{4}}{{n}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2{n}^{3}}{{n}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n}{(2+\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n}{2+0} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n\n- In sequence III, the dominant term in the denominator is $5n^4,$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by $n^4$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{3{n}^{5}+7}{5{n}^{4}-3{n}^{3}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3{n}^{5}}{{n}^{4}}+\\frac{7}{{n}^{4}})}{(\\frac{5{n}^{4}}{{n}^{4}}-\\frac{3{n}^{3}}{{n}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(3n+\\frac{7}{{n}^{4}})}{(5-\\frac{3}{n})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{3n+0}{5-0} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n\nIn conclusion, sequences II and III diverge." 13194139535283 true] [17592186096470 1145 "Let's analyze each sequence in turn. We need to calculate the limit of each sequence as $n$ approaches at infinity.\n\n- In sequence I, the limit is\n$\\displaystyle \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} a_n = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\dfrac {1}{n^2} = 0$.\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n- In sequence II, the dominant term in the denominator is $2n^3$, so we divide the numerator and the denominator by $n^3$ and get\n$\\displaystyle \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}a_{n}= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{n^{4}}{2n^{3} + 1} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{(\\frac{n^{4}}{n^{3}})}{(\\frac{2n^{3}}{n^{3}} + \\frac{1}{n^{3}})} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{n}{(2 + \\frac{1}{n^{3}})} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{n}{2 + 0} = \\infty$.\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n- In sequence III, the dominant term in the denominator is $5n^4$, so we divide the numerator and the denominator by $n^4$ and get\n$\\displaystyle \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}a_{n}= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{3n^{5} + 7}{5n^{4} - 3n^{3}} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{(\\frac{3n^{5}}{n^{4}} + \\frac{7}{n^{4}})}{(\\frac{5n^{4}}{n^{4}} - \\frac{3n^{3}}{n^{4}})} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{(3n + \\frac{7}{n^{4}})}{(5 - \\frac{3}{n})} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{3n + 0}{5 - 0} = \\infty$.\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n\nIn conclusion, sequences II and III diverge." 13194139535283 false] [17592186096471 1100 "Does the sequence $a_n = \\dfrac {3 n ^ 5 - n} {5 n ^ 6  - n}$ for $n\\geq 1$ converge or diverge? If the sequence converges, what is its limit?" 13194139535283 true] [17592186096471 1100 "Does the sequence $a_n = \\dfrac {3 n ^ 5 - n} {5 n ^ 6 - n}$ for $n\\geq 1$ converge or diverge? If the sequence converges, what is its limit?" 13194139535283 false] [17592186096471 1145 "To determine whether  the sequence converges or diverges, we need to determine the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} a_n = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\dfrac {3 n ^ 5 - n} {5 n ^ 6  - n}\n$$\n\nThe dominant term in the denominator is $5n^6,$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by $n^6$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{3{n}^{5}-n}{5{n}^{6}-n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3{n}^{5}}{{n}^{6}}-\\frac{n}{{n}^{6}})}{(\\frac{5{n}^{6}}{{n}^{6}}-\\frac{n}{{n}^{6}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3}{n}-\\frac{1}{{n}^{5}})}{(5-\\frac{1}{{n}^{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0}{5-0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the limit exists, the sequence converges, and its limit is $0.$" 13194139535283 true] [17592186096471 1145 "To determine whether the sequence converges or diverges, we need to determine the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} a_n = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\dfrac {3 n ^ 5 - n} {5 n ^ 6 - n}\n$$\n\nThe dominant term in the denominator is $5n^6$, so we divide the numerator and the denominator by $n^6$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{3n^{5} - n}{5n^{6} - n} &= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{(\\frac{3n^{5}}{n^{6}} - \\frac{n}{n^{6}})}{(\\frac{5n^{6}}{n^{6}} - \\frac{n}{n^{6}})} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{(\\frac{3}{n} - \\frac{1}{n^{5}})}{(5 - \\frac{1}{n^{5}})} \\\\\n&= \\frac{0 - 0}{5 - 0} \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the limit exists, the sequence converges, and its limit is $0$." 13194139535283 false] [17592186096472 1100 "What is the limit of the sequence $a_n = \\dfrac {n(3n-7)} {(3n-1)(3n+1)}$ for $n\\geq 1$?" 13194139535283 false] [17592186096472 1100 "What is the limit of the sequence $a_n = \\dfrac {n(3n-7)} {(3n-1)(3n+1)}$ for $n\\geq 1?$" 13194139535283 true] [17592186096472 1145 "First, we multiply out the numerator and denominator of the sequence and get\n\n$$\na_n=\\dfrac {n(3n-7)} {(3n-1)(3n+1)}=\\dfrac {3 n ^ 2 - 7 n} {9 n ^ 2-1}\n$$\n\nSo to find the limit, we will need to compute\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} a_n = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\dfrac {3 n ^ 2 - 7 n} {9 n ^ 2-1}\n$$\n\nThe dominant term in the denominator is $n^2$, so we divide the numerator and the denominator by $n^2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{3n^{2} - 7n}{9n^{2} - 1} &= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{(\\frac{3n^{2}}{n^{2}} - \\frac{7n}{n^{2}})}{(\\frac{9n^{2}}{n^{2}} - \\frac{1}{n^{2}})} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\frac{(3 - \\frac{7}{n})}{(9 - \\frac{1}{n^{2}})} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3 - 0}{9 - 0} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the sequence converges and its limit is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 3\n$$" 13194139535283 false] [17592186096472 1145 "First, we multiply out the numerator and denominator of the sequence and get\n\n$$\na_n=\\dfrac {n(3n-7)} {(3n-1)(3n+1)}=\\dfrac {3 n ^ 2 - 7 n} {9 n ^ 2-1}.\n$$\n\nSo to find the limit, we will need to compute\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} a_n = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty}  \\dfrac {3 n ^ 2 - 7 n} {9 n ^ 2-1}.\n$$\n\nThe dominant term in the denominator is $n^2,$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by $n^2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{3{n}^{2}-7n}{9{n}^{2}-1} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3{n}^{2}}{{n}^{2}}-\\frac{7n}{{n}^{2}})}{(\\frac{9{n}^{2}}{{n}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(3-\\frac{7}{n})}{(9-\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-0}{9-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the sequence converges and its limit is $\\dfrac 1 3.$" 13194139535283 true] [17592186096660 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341556 13194139535283 true] [17592186096660 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341577 13194139535283 true] [17592186096660 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341584 13194139535283 true] [17592186096660 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341605 13194139535283 true] [17592186096661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341563 13194139535283 true] [17592186096661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341570 13194139535283 true] [17592186096661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341612 13194139535283 true] [17592186096661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341616 13194139535283 true] [17592186096661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341619 13194139535283 true] [17592186096663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341591 13194139535283 true] [17592186096663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341598 13194139535283 true] [17592186096663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341622 13194139535283 true] [17592186096663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341626 13194139535283 true] [17592186096663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341629 13194139535283 true] [17592186097272 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535283 true] [17592186097272 1100 "Which of the following sequences diverge?\n\n- ${a}_{n}=\\frac{n-1}{{n}^{3}+1}$ for $n\\ge 1$\n- ${a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{{n}^{3}}$ for $n\\ge 1$\n- ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}+3}{3{n}^{2}-n}$ for $n\\ge 1$" 13194139535283 true] [17592186097272 1100 "Which of the following sequences diverge?\n\n1. $a_{n} = \\frac{n - 1}{n^{3} + 1}$ for $n \\ge 1$\n2. $a_{n} = \\frac{2}{n^{3}}$ for $n \\ge 1$\n3. $a_{n} = \\frac{n^{3} + 3}{3n^{2} - n}$ for $n \\ge 1$" 13194139535283 false] [17592186097272 1145 "Let's analyze each sequence in turn. We need to calculate the limit of each sequence as $n$ approaches at infinity.\n\n- In sequence I, the dominant term in the denominator is ${n}^{3},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n-1}{{n}^{3}+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }⁡\\frac{(\\frac{n}{{n}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{n}^{3}}{{n}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }⁡\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})}{(1+\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0}{1+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\n- In sequence II, the limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{2}{{n}^{3}}=0.\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\n- In sequence III, the dominant term in the denominator is $3{n}^{2},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}+3}{3{n}^{2}-n} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{n}^{3}}{{n}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{{n}^{2}})}{(\\frac{3{n}^{2}}{{n}^{2}}-\\frac{n}{{n}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(n+\\frac{3}{{n}^{2}})}{(3-\\frac{1}{n})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n+0}{3-0} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n\nIn conclusion, sequence III diverges." 13194139535283 true] [17592186341556 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341557 13194139535283 true] [17592186341556 1089 "q-11154" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341556 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535283 true] [17592186341556 1100 "What is the limit of the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{1-{n}^{4}}{3{n}^{2}+5}$ for $n\\ge 1?$" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341556 1113 #uuid "0b30fa3e-ef1b-5f57-b24f-ec927f3f408c" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341556 1145 "The dominant term  in the denominator is $3{n}^{2}$, so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{1-{n}^{4}}{3{n}^{2}+5} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}-\\frac{{n}^{4}}{{n}^{2}})}{(\\frac{3{n}^{2}}{{n}^{2}}+\\frac{5}{{n}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}-{n}^{2})}{(3+\\frac{5}{{n}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{0-{n}^{2}}{3+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{{n}^{2}}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges." 13194139535283 true] [17592186341557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341558 13194139535283 true] [17592186341557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341559 13194139535283 true] [17592186341557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341560 13194139535283 true] [17592186341557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341561 13194139535283 true] [17592186341557 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341562 13194139535283 true] [17592186341557 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535283 true] [17592186341557 1041 "selection" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341557 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341559 13194139535283 true] [17592186341557 1110 #uuid "a85e1bd3-040f-5ccb-aa26-1c129ffd5afc" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341558 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535283 true] [17592186341558 1111 #uuid "823826ce-1713-5441-8686-686e66458119" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341559 1034 "The sequence diverges." 13194139535283 true] [17592186341559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535283 true] [17592186341559 1111 #uuid "3d71fdc5-6d02-57dd-85b5-36f6c371164d" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341560 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535283 true] [17592186341560 1111 #uuid "cdc43ca8-943c-5b4f-af45-6787b037bc38" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341561 1034 "0" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535283 true] [17592186341561 1111 #uuid "d86b1d00-6644-5b21-9af1-0ea73b71dc65" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341562 1034 "-1" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535283 true] [17592186341562 1111 #uuid "ec293fa6-8b08-5f63-b961-b3daa7506e2c" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341563 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341564 13194139535283 true] [17592186341563 1089 "q-123307" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341563 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535283 true] [17592186341563 1100 "What is the limit of the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{3{n}^{4}-{n}^{2}}{5-2{n}^{4}}$ for $n\\ge 1?$" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341563 1113 #uuid "a0169118-d896-5b32-afd4-00c3a6b643ef" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341563 1145 "To determine whether the sequence converges or diverges, we need to determine the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=\\frac{3{n}^{4}-{n}^{2}}{5-2{n}^{4}}.\n$$\n\nThe dominant term in the denominator is $-2{n}^{4},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{3{n}^{4}-{n}^{2}}{5-2{n}^{4}} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3{n}^{4}}{{n}^{4}}-\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{n}^{4}})}{(\\frac{5}{{n}^{4}}-\\frac{2{n}^{4}}{{n}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(3-\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}})}{\\frac{5}{{n}^{4}}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-0}{0-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the limit exists, the sequence converges, and its limit is $-\\frac{3}{2}.$" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341565 13194139535283 true] [17592186341564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341566 13194139535283 true] [17592186341564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341567 13194139535283 true] [17592186341564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341568 13194139535283 true] [17592186341564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341569 13194139535283 true] [17592186341564 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535283 true] [17592186341564 1041 "selection" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341564 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341567 13194139535283 true] [17592186341564 1110 #uuid "1e3c0b7d-79cb-5642-a3e6-471c54a2db1a" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341565 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341565 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535283 true] [17592186341565 1111 #uuid "4c0334f7-22e9-574c-843f-ed0a18569bcd" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341566 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341566 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535283 true] [17592186341566 1111 #uuid "c7dd59e2-d0c1-5f54-bd26-ccf67456fce8" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341567 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535283 true] [17592186341567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535283 true] [17592186341567 1111 #